        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0474" n="1128" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg1128"/>

                <head>No. 538.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cushing to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-06-29"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 29, 1875</date>.
                        (Received July 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 431.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We are, according to all appearances, on
                    the eve of interesting events, military and political, of which report will be
                    transmitted in due time.</p>
                <p>A decree of this date, ordering the retaliatory confiscation of the property of
                    Carlists, is annexed in copy and translation, as one of the indications of a new
                    stage in the war between the government of Spain and its rebellious
                    provinces.</p>
                <p>I call attention to the circumstance that, in the prefatory exposition, the
                    minister of gohernacion cites and relies upon the example of the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>C. CUSHING.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d239-a1.xml" xpointer="d239-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
